WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:03.850
Abraham: Now that you have conducted
your personal skills analysis and

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:08.189
assessed the skills you have against
various roles in cyber security it is

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:11.990
time to create a personal development
plan, to help you decide what you

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.410
need to do in order to achieve your
goal of working in cyber security.

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:18.919
Nicole: To do this you should
use SMART goals or targets.

00:00:19.299 --> 00:00:20.639
So, what exactly are these?

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:23.329
SMART is an acronym which stands for

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:28.820
Abraham: Specific, Measurable,
Achievable, Relevant, Timebound.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.249
Nicole: Specific means each goal or
target should be clear and focussed

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.850
on what you want to accomplish.

00:00:35.389 --> 00:00:39.199
Think about why it is important,
who is involved, where will it

00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:41.659
happen what resources are needed!

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:42.179
For example:

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.710
Abraham: ‘I want to be able to
gain the experience and skills

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.110
to become a team leader in cyber
security within my organisation’

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:54.080
Nicole: Measurable is a way of tracking
your progress and keeping motivated.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.950
It should ask questions like ‘how
will I know that I am on track to

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.480
do this?’ And ‘what will I need
to do to help make it happen?’ Try

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.520
setting a timeline for your progress.

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:09.050
Abraham: Achievable means that the
goals and targets you set are realistic.

00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:13.289
By breaking down your goals into smaller
steps can make them easier to achieve.

00:01:13.969 --> 00:01:16.660
Don’t forget we all have to
walk before we try to run!

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:20.289
Think about how long some of the
skills you need may take to get

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.210
and remember set goals that you can
control and are not down to others.

00:01:24.889 --> 00:01:27.929
Nicole: Relevant is about making
sure that you goal means something

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:32.560
to you, and it really matters, is
worthwhile and achievable at this time.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.860
Abraham: Time-bound is all about
setting target dates giving you

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.230
something to focus on and work towards.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.880
These should be realistic and are best
broken down into smaller goals and

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.819
remember don’t be too specific, if
something is worth doing it’s worth

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.719
doing well and shouldn’t be rushed.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:53.559
Nicole: And finally, it’s always
worthwhile factoring in contingencies

00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:57.489
as we are all well aware of what
can happen when we least expect it!

